### 🐛 Current behavior

When using `<InstantSearchNext routing={true}>` Algolia will correctly display search hits for a query when it is passed as an url param like `mypage.com/search?query=stuff` (assuming that an app router page named `search` exists, that mounts InstantSearchNext). But the `query` param gets dropped from the URL upon hydration.

We're currently using the following workaround to always add the query to the URL, if it exists:

```tsx
    <InstantSearchNext 
        routing={{
            router: {
                createURL({ qsModule, location, routeState }) {
                    const { origin, pathname, hash } = location;
                    const queryString = qsModule.stringify({
                        ...(query && { query }),
                        ...routeState,
                    });

                    return `${origin}${pathname}?${queryString}${hash}`;
                },
            },
        }}
    >
```

### 🔍 Steps to reproduce

The `query` url param gets deleted upon hydration when using the default router. Setting/changing the filters/sorting settings will work and will correctly be persisted in the URL - only the search query param doesn't.

### Live reproduction

no sandbox for InstantSearchNext available

### 💭 Expected behavior

The `query` param should persist in the URL when using the default router.

### Package version

react-instantsearch: 7.16.1, react-instantsearch-nextjs: 1.0.0

